Great clarification! You want the message section to:

- **Auto-expand** as more messages are added (height increases gradually).
- **Stop expanding at a certain height**.
- Then **enable scroll**, rather than showing a scroll from the start.

This is commonly done using **max-height** and **overflow-y-auto**. I’ll show you how to modify the **message display area** so that it grows with content naturally until a set limit, after which it becomes scrollable.

---

### ✅ Here's the updated **Messages Section** code:
Make this change in your **"Messages Section"** (`Send Text Message` section):

```jsx
{/* Messages Section */}
<div className="bg-gray-800/80 backdrop-blur-sm border border-gray-700/50 p-6 rounded-xl shadow-2xl flex flex-col">
  <h2 className="text-lg font-semibold mb-4">Send Text Message</h2>

  {/* Textarea Input */}
  <textarea
    value={message}
    onChange={(e) => setMessage(e.target.value)}
    onKeyDown={handleKeyPress}
    placeholder="Type your message (Ctrl+Enter to send)"
    rows={4}
    className="w-full p-3 bg-gray-700 border border-gray-600 rounded-lg focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-indigo-500 resize-none"
  />

  {/* Dynamic message display area (Auto-expand & scroll after max height) */}
  {sentMessages?.length > 0 && (
    <div className="mt-4 bg-gray-700/50 border border-gray-600/50 rounded-lg p-4 overflow-y-auto"
         style={{ maxHeight: '300px' }}>
      <div className="space-y-2">
        {sentMessages.map((msg, idx) => (
          <p
            key={idx}
            className="text-sm text-gray-100 bg-gray-800 px-3 py-2 rounded-md break-words"
          >
            {msg}
          </p>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  )}

  {/* Send Button */}
  <button
    onClick={sendTextMessage}
    disabled={!message.trim() || !connectionRef.current}
    className="mt-4 w-full px-4 py-3 bg-green-600 hover:bg-green-700 disabled:bg-gray-600 disabled:cursor-not-allowed rounded-lg transition-colors"
  >
    Send Message
  </button>
</div>
```

---

### 🧠 Key Changes & Styling Concepts:

| Feature              | Code / Explanation |
|----------------------|--------------------|
| **Container growth** | `maxHeight: '300px'` allows natural growth till 300px. |
| **Scroll after limit** | `overflow-y-auto` ensures scroll **only after** max height is reached. |
| **Better display** | Each message wrapped in a `<p>` with styling for readability. |
| **Conditionally render** | Only show message box if `sentMessages.length > 0`. |

---

### 💡 Optional Improvement:
Keep a `sentMessages` array in state as:

```js
const [sentMessages, setSentMessages] = useState([]);
```

Then update it when a message is sent:

```js
const sendTextMessage = () => {
  if (!message.trim() || !connectionRef.current) return;
  connectionRef.current.send(message);
  setSentMessages((prev) => [...prev, message]); // Add message to history
  setMessage(""); // Clear input
  setStatusMessage("Message sent!");
};
```

---

### ✅ Final Result:
The **messages view grows taller** naturally as more messages are typed or sent, and **only begins scrolling** after it reaches the predefined `max-height`, giving users a smoother, space-efficient experience.

